WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
A headliner takes over the rostrum at the National Press Club in Washington.

00:08.000 --> 00:13.000
The men who cover the capital scene are regaled by Alfred Hitchcock, the master of suspense,

00:13.000 --> 00:17.000
who has some comments about his latest picture.

00:17.000 --> 00:27.000
For over 30 years now, I have been indulging in the occupation of raising goose flesh domestically and in England.

00:27.000 --> 00:31.000
I have only recently completed work on the latest picture.

00:31.000 --> 00:35.000
The title is quite short, just two words.

00:35.000 --> 00:44.000
There were three, but we cut the first word, four,

00:44.000 --> 00:52.000
and call it simply The Birds.

00:52.000 --> 01:01.000
Naturally, most of the actors in The Birds are.

01:01.000 --> 01:10.000
In fact, I have employed more feathered performers than have been seen since pan dancing went out of style.

01:10.000 --> 01:14.000
The cast also includes a few men and women.

01:14.000 --> 01:24.000
All in all, the picture isn't just about the birds, it's about the bees too.

01:24.000 --> 01:29.000
Mr. Hitchcock receives a citation to mark his 30 years of contribution to the world of entertainment.

01:29.000 --> 01:31.000
The Birds is his 50th movie.

01:31.000 --> 01:48.000
The honors for the man who was chilling movie audiences long before air conditioning.

